{"chunk_id":"R3-241529-001","collection":"ran3_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["Nokia"],"tdocNumber":"R3-241529","title":"Discussion on LTM when NR-DC is Configured"},"point_id":"8625243751899202267"}
In regard to L1/L2 triggered mobility (LTM), a new Work Item has been approved (RP-234036 NR mobility enhancements Phase 4), including the following related objectives and scope impacting RAN3: This paper highlights LTM dual connectivity related aspects to be discussed in the scope of Rel-19. LTM when NR-DC is configured is part of the objectives of Rel-19 WID for inter-CU LTM work. In TS 37.340, different multi-connectivity scenarios and their respective signalling for PSCell addition, change, release or retention are described. These cell changes or reconfigurations can be MN or SN initiated. Likewise, in Rel-18 various issues related to inter-SN PSCell change were discussed and agreements were made under S-CPAC feature that could be considered for LTM work in Rel-19. Observation 1: In Rel-18 various issues related to inter-SN PSCell change were discussed and agreements were made under S-CPAC feature. Proposal 1: RAN3 to study whether and to what extent the Rel-18 S-CPAC framework could be re-used in context for LTM when NR-DC is configured in Rel-19. The following are NR-DC scenarios applicable for Rel-19 work scope: Inter-MN PCell change With SCG released With SCG retained Inter-SN PSCell change with unchanged PCell MN initiated SN initiated Based on WID [1] scope, the scenario of “Inter-SN PSCell change with simultaneous PCell change” is excluded from Rel-19 work. Proposal 2: RAN3 to prioritize the NR-DC scenarios to be specified under inter-CU LTM work in Rel-19. An additional aspect is in regard the Note in the Rel-19 WID description [1], which indicates the following: This Note is ambiguous and can be interpreted in different ways, such as (Interpretation 1) In Rel-19 simultaneous MCG and SCG LTM configuration shall be deprioritized. (Interpretation 2) In Rel-19 simultaneous MCG and SCG LTM configuration shall not be supported. Proposal 3: RAN3 to clarify understanding of the meaning of the note in inter0CU LTM WID that indicates “The case that LTM is configured in both MCG and SCG is excluded”.

